the Maecenas Universitatis Corvini Foundation, Corvinus’ medium-term objective is to become the best higher education institution in these fields, not only in the country but also in Central Europe. Corvinus University currently has around 8,000 students, including 2,000 international students. It has close links with more than 250 partner universities worldwide. Corvinus regularly ranks highly in international higher education rankings, and its Business and Management programme was ranked first in the region in the 2019 Eduniversal ranking. Corvinus University of Budapest is the only university in Hungary in the field of economics to hold two international accreditations (AMBA, AACSB). The Institute of Accounting and Law announces an open call for applications for the position of Associate Professor (full-time) on a fixed-term (two-year) contract, with a focus on secondary school economics teacher education. Earliest expected start date: 1 December 2026. Job description Teaching duties: Teaching courses within the Institute’s teaching portfolio, in the number of weekly contact hours defined by the University’s Academic Career Model. Developing and enhancing the course portfolio of the secondary school economics teacher training programme (Teacher of Economics, MA). Teaching subject-pedagogy courses (methodology of teaching economics), supervising school-based teaching practice and supervising master’s theses. Research duties: Publishing in leading international and Hungarian peer-reviewed journals in the fields of economics education, subject pedagogy and teacher education. Presenting at major international and Hungarian conferences, building international academic networks, participating in research projects and actively applying for research grants in economics education and teacher education, thereby securing funding for research and contributing to the internationalisation of the Institute and the University. Service duties: Active participation in the academic life of the Institute and the University, and performing service tasks assigned by the Head of Institute. Supporting early-career academics at the University, and supervising PhD students as well as students participating in academic competitions. Mentoring assistant professors in the Institute. Acting as programme coordinator of the economics teacher training programme. Developing the strategy and curricula of the secondary school teacher training centre. Building and maintaining partnerships with partner schools and mentor teachers involved in school-based teaching practice. Contributing to the establishment of the examination centre for regulated professions (in the fields of accounting and law). Basic requirements a PhD degree obtained at least three years ago; a degree in education (pedagogy) or a teaching qualification, preferably in economics; a PhD in educational science or economics education is an advantage; secondary school teaching experience, preferably in economics or business subjects, is an advantage; relevant teaching and research experience in higher education, preferably in teacher education; an outstanding teaching and research record in their field; a record of independent research; the ability to teach in both Hungarian and English, and to act as a course leader. Documents and certificates to be submitted as part of the application Application in English (a single PDF file) containing: a detailed curriculum vitae (CV) summarising teaching, research and academic service achievements; a cover letter outlining the applicant’s motivation and intended contribution to the Institute’s work, in particular to economics teacher education, and stating their gross salary expectations; scanned copies of the documents certifying university degrees, academic degrees (e.g. PhD) and other professional qualifications, including teaching qualifications (for academic degrees obtained abroad, nostrification will be arranged at a later stage of the selection procedure); up to two publications , preferably in economics education or teacher education (working papers, doctoral dissertations and job market papers are also accepted); at least two professional references (one of which must be from a Hungarian expert if the call is published in Hungarian); results of the applicant’s previous student evaluations of teaching ; Remuneration and benefits favourable research conditions, including research facilities and data access; dedicated research time, travel support, etc.; a competitive salary, complemented by an annual performance bonus of up to 15% for outstanding performance; one-off relocation allowance for applicants moving to Hungary; cafeteria (flexible fringe benefit) scheme; place of work: Budapest. Application procedure Application deadline: 22 October 2026. Applications must be submitted electronically by clicking the APPLICATION button and following the instructions at the bottom of the webpage. Shortlisted applicants will be interviewed by the selection committee ; they will be informed of the details and timing in due course. The evaluation of applications is expected to be completed by 13 November 2026. APPLICATION For further information: Please contact us by email: administrative and HR matters: career@uni-corvinus.hu academic matters: janos.lukacs@uni-corvinus.hu , lakatos@uni-corvinus.hu Copied to clipboard Manage Consent To provide the best experiences, we use technologies like cookies to store and/or access device information. Consenting to these technologies will allow us to process data such as browsing behavior or unique IDs on this site. Not consenting or withdrawing consent, may adversely affect certain features and functions. Functional Functional Always active The technical storage or access is strictly necessary for the legitimate purpose of enabling the use of a specific service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user, or for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network. Preferences Preferences The technical storage or access is necessary for the legitimate purpose of storing preferences that are not requested by the subscriber or user. Statistics Statistics The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for statistical purposes. The technical storage or access that is used exclusively for anonymous statistical purposes. Without a subpoena, voluntary compliance on the part of your Internet Service Provider, or additional records from a third party, information stored or retrieved for this purpose alone cannot usually be used to identify you. Marketing Marketing The technical storage or access is required to create user profiles to send advertising, or to track the user on a website or across several websites for similar marketing purposes. Manage options Manage services Manage {vendor_count} vendors Read more about these purposes Accept Deny View preferences Save preferences View preferences {title} {title} {title} Manage consent Contact Us Telephone: +36 1 482 5000 Do you have questions about the admissions? Academic Contacts For current students HUB Press: press@uni-corvinus.hu Useful information Opening Hours House Rules Public Data Career at Corvinus Design Elements RRF Public data Follow us Facebook LinkedIn Youtube Instagram TikTok X International accreditations Main international memberships Cookie & Data Management Settings Policy © Corvinus University of Budapest ×"
